CI note: COMMAND-HUB-GUARDRAILS.yml's `pull_request` trigger has no
`types:` override, so it defaults to [opened, synchronize, reopened] and
does not include `edited` — unlike VALIDATOR-CHECK.yml. Its
"Path Ownership Guard" job therefore keeps evaluating the PR title as it
stood at the last push/reopen; adding the required DEV-COMHU-03712 marker
via a title-only edit does not by itself trigger a fresh run. This commit
(a real evidence-pack addition, not a no-op) is what re-fires it via a
genuine `synchronize` event against the current (DEV-COMHU-03712-bearing)
PR title.
